{"id": 44, "ts": 1780462862.5303166, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I agree with Sarah and James that Candidate\u202fC remains the strongest overall, but I want to highlight a gap that could shift our view: Candidate\u202fC\u2019s technical and cognitive competence is not documented. While his 100\u202f% reliability, rapid correct decisions, and positive crew atmosphere cover reliability, decision quality, and crew cooperation, we have no evidence that he can understand complex aircraft systems or manage high\u2011workload tasks\u2014key for long\u2011distance operations. In contrast, Candidate\u202fA shows concrete strengths in anticipating dangerous situations, seeing complex connections, and excellent spatial vision, which directly speak to technical competence and situational awareness, even though we lack stress\u2011resilience data. If we value technical depth, A could be a viable alternative. Therefore, I still vote for Candidate\u202fC, but I recommend we obtain at least one concrete example of C\u2019s technical competence before finalizing."}
