{"id": 48, "ts": 1780462908.2076912, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is our best choice. Emily rightly points out the lack of documented technical and cognitive competence for C, but we must weigh that against the concrete safety\u2011critical strengths we do have: 100\u202f% operational reliability, rapid correct decision\u2011making, and a demonstrably positive crew atmosphere. Those directly satisfy the core criteria of reliability, decision quality, and crew cooperation for long\u2011distance flights. In contrast, Candidate\u202fA, while showing strong technical awareness (anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision), has no evidence of stress resilience or calmness under pressure, and is perceived as a \u201cshow\u2011off\u201d and \u201cnot open to new ideas,\u201d which raises serious concerns about reliability and adaptability. The risks associated with A\u2019s teamwork and attitude are harder to mitigate than the technical gap for C, which can be addressed through targeted training and mentorship. Therefore, I continue to vote for Candidate\u202fC."}
